SUMMARY:Special Event: Whose Turn Is It
LOCATION:Helium Comedy Club\, 10 W. Georgia St.\, Portland
DESCRIPTION:We blew the roof off Philly before PAX Unplugged so now we’re
  bringing the chaos to Gen Con 2026 . The night before the con\, Helium Ind
 ianapolis becomes the tavern at the edge of the multiverse as Kiwi legend S
 teve Wrigley stand‑up comic\, Dungeon Master\, and the internet’s favor
 ite TTRPG crowd‑wrangler returns with a one‑night‑only comedy brawl i
 nspired by last year’s smash‑hit show.\n\nTwo teams enter. Only one lea
 ves with bragging rights. It’s fast\, funny\, and gloriously unhinged as 
 Steve leads a cast of comedians\, creators\, and tabletop misfits through a
  night of unscripted mayhem pulled straight from the culture of TTRPGs.\n\n
 Also returning to the fray is team leader Jay Foster \, the powerhouse behi
 nd Oops All Himbos and one of the most beloved voices in the TTRPG media sp
 ace. Jay’s razor‑sharp wit and genre‑bending humor helped make the Ph
 illy show legendary and this Gen Con rematch promises even bigger laughs.\n
 \nIf you’re rolling into Indy early or just riding the pre‑con hype wav
 e this is your official warm‑up. Comedy\, chaos\, and critical hits. More
  guests to be announced. Bags down\, dice up. The night before Gen Con star
 ts here.\n\nCouples Package includes:\n\n- 2 premium seats\n- $90 food & be
 verage credit ($45 per person)\n- Gratuity\n- Ticket Protection\n\n**The Pr
 ivate Skybox Suite includes up to 10 tickets\, a $400 Food & Beverage vouch
 er\, a personal server\, a private restroom\, and all gratuity charges.\n\n
 Any additional food and drink costs above $400 will be billed at the end of
  the show. The guest count can not exceed 10 people. All club policies and 
 safety guidelines will be enforced. Please note that the skybox is on the s
 econd floor of our showroom\, and is NOT wheelchair accessible.\nMore info:
  https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/special-event-whose-turn-is-it/
